[{:db/id 17592186124490 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f5e736f9-a7fd-5964-86e8-9e7f4c30d97a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f5e736f9-a7fd-5964-86e8-9e7f4c30d97a" :question/id #uuid "f5e736f9-a7fd-5964-86e8-9e7f4c30d97a" :question/math-academy-id "q-35254" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$, where $x\\in {R}^{3}$, is a basis of ${R}^{2}$\n\nII. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},4{b}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n\nIII. $\\{{c}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{2}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}(4{b}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+(4{x}_{3}){b}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},4{b}_{3}\\}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},4{b}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+\\frac{{x}_{3}}{4}(4{b}_{3})\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The set $\\{{c}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$ because the set consists of all the vectors from the basis $C$ written in a different order.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-399a1def-da95-5c7b-b07c-dd77153c4399"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-399a1def-da95-5c7b-b07c-dd77153c4399" :answer-field/id #uuid "399a1def-da95-5c7b-b07c-dd77153c4399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ff9d9bd-25c1-553b-af23-b5a3804fa12a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ebabf65-87a9-50c0-a00e-9f63618f09de" "answer-99988b28-0eb3-5cc7-aaa9-88164b97c763" "answer-9ff9d9bd-25c1-553b-af23-b5a3804fa12a" "answer-26aab52f-ff38-5268-9e76-730ae0da1260" "answer-2c393b44-730a-5f93-9acb-fbe9996ca594"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ebabf65-87a9-50c0-a00e-9f63618f09de" :answer/id #uuid "4ebabf65-87a9-50c0-a00e-9f63618f09de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99988b28-0eb3-5cc7-aaa9-88164b97c763" :answer/id #uuid "99988b28-0eb3-5cc7-aaa9-88164b97c763" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ff9d9bd-25c1-553b-af23-b5a3804fa12a" :answer/id #uuid "9ff9d9bd-25c1-553b-af23-b5a3804fa12a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26aab52f-ff38-5268-9e76-730ae0da1260" :answer/id #uuid "26aab52f-ff38-5268-9e76-730ae0da1260" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c393b44-730a-5f93-9acb-fbe9996ca594" :answer/id #uuid "2c393b44-730a-5f93-9acb-fbe9996ca594" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124489 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8e6a690a-1af9-54cd-96d8-6699f35c43cf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e6a690a-1af9-54cd-96d8-6699f35c43cf" :question/id #uuid "8e6a690a-1af9-54cd-96d8-6699f35c43cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-94865" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nII. $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that all linear combinations of \n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nresult in matrices with the entry ${a}_{21}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ can't be written as a linear combination of the set, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20236f24-a672-571d-8a2d-4eb8e53f4a42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20236f24-a672-571d-8a2d-4eb8e53f4a42" :answer-field/id #uuid "20236f24-a672-571d-8a2d-4eb8e53f4a42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b2c106c-830c-550f-9834-4e30ffa6398f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70454c64-8842-5c74-90d5-a65a027e02d1" "answer-a2106cd2-d4c4-5485-bd50-b22dc45d0703" "answer-5b2c106c-830c-550f-9834-4e30ffa6398f" "answer-9b5a2ff6-779a-5eee-95b7-e7c15c73d9b5" "answer-d51926b0-1f7a-5517-b205-7d50c8ea1fd2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70454c64-8842-5c74-90d5-a65a027e02d1" :answer/id #uuid "70454c64-8842-5c74-90d5-a65a027e02d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2106cd2-d4c4-5485-bd50-b22dc45d0703" :answer/id #uuid "a2106cd2-d4c4-5485-bd50-b22dc45d0703" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b2c106c-830c-550f-9834-4e30ffa6398f" :answer/id #uuid "5b2c106c-830c-550f-9834-4e30ffa6398f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b5a2ff6-779a-5eee-95b7-e7c15c73d9b5" :answer/id #uuid "9b5a2ff6-779a-5eee-95b7-e7c15c73d9b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d51926b0-1f7a-5517-b205-7d50c8ea1fd2" :answer/id #uuid "d51926b0-1f7a-5517-b205-7d50c8ea1fd2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b133af0b-64de-5a69-afba-ce5e85bd85f5" :activity/id #uuid "b133af0b-64de-5a69-afba-ce5e85bd85f5" :activity/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048552 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-7517e0b5-948e-589e-82bc-4f03c404dd2f" "step-fc090e22-1e8a-579b-9615-543cf7ef59c3" "step-b752cd7b-1282-56eb-b8ed-21c8bfb9825b" "step-863020c7-988a-55d4-89e2-3c40430f3b22" "step-91cfcf29-baa9-52fa-a889-0d9f790d046b"] :activity/first-step "step-7517e0b5-948e-589e-82bc-4f03c404dd2f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7517e0b5-948e-589e-82bc-4f03c404dd2f" :step/id #uuid "7517e0b5-948e-589e-82bc-4f03c404dd2f" :step/content "question-f5e736f9-a7fd-5964-86e8-9e7f4c30d97a" :step/next "step-fc090e22-1e8a-579b-9615-543cf7ef59c3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fc090e22-1e8a-579b-9615-543cf7ef59c3" :step/id #uuid "fc090e22-1e8a-579b-9615-543cf7ef59c3" :step/content 17592186406883 :step/next "step-b752cd7b-1282-56eb-b8ed-21c8bfb9825b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b752cd7b-1282-56eb-b8ed-21c8bfb9825b" :step/id #uuid "b752cd7b-1282-56eb-b8ed-21c8bfb9825b" :step/content "question-8e6a690a-1af9-54cd-96d8-6699f35c43cf" :step/next "step-863020c7-988a-55d4-89e2-3c40430f3b22" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-863020c7-988a-55d4-89e2-3c40430f3b22" :step/id #uuid "863020c7-988a-55d4-89e2-3c40430f3b22" :step/content 17592186244046 :step/next "step-91cfcf29-baa9-52fa-a889-0d9f790d046b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-91cfcf29-baa9-52fa-a889-0d9f790d046b" :step/id #uuid "91cfcf29-baa9-52fa-a889-0d9f790d046b" :step/content 17592186244069 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229193 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bee016d0-6cd7-5398-ae5a-81f82544f72f" "question-e29b2a6a-e1e7-5fde-b63b-dc98de03f40b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228884 :question/problem "Find $160\\%$ of $75,$ and then $150\\%$ of the result." :question/worked-solution "First, we find $160\\%$ of $75{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}160%\\times 75 & =\\frac{160}{100}\\times 75 \\\\  & =1.6\\times 75 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $150\\%$ of the result $(120){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}150%\\times 120 & =\\frac{150}{100}\\times 120 \\\\  & =1.5\\times 120 \\\\  & =180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $180.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229194 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-311706e9-5725-57d0-9ebd-1cb5c9f7c783" "question-7e4472fc-358a-5367-8f2d-7c530ac4418c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228882 :question/problem "A service adjusted a subscription fee to $90\\%$ of its original cost. A surcharge of $18\\%$ was applied to the adjusted fee. If the subscription originally cost $\\[math]180,$ what is the surcharge?" :question/worked-solution "First, the adjusted fee is $90\\%$ of the original cost $(\\[math]180){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}90%\\times 180 & =\\frac{90}{100}\\times 180 \\\\  & =0.9\\times 180 \\\\  & =162\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the adjusted fee is $\\[/math]162.$ Then, the surcharge is $18\\%$ of this fee:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18%\\times 162 & =\\frac{18}{100}\\times 162 \\\\  & =0.18\\times 162 \\\\  & =29.16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surcharge is $\\[math]29.16.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229195 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3a5e4afd-b3bf-55da-bca0-9104ea0bafe7" "question-786bda33-d02b-5551-a3f5-7adb0032f21a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228877 :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the total number of viewers.\n\nWe're told that $40\\%$ of viewers enjoyed documentaries. Thus, the number of viewers who enjoy documentaries is \n\n$$\n0.4x.\n$$\n\nWe are also told that of those viewers who enjoy documentaries, $50\\%$ preferred nature topics. So, the number of viewers who preferred nature documentaries is\n\n$$\n0.50(0.4x) = 0.20x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.20x$ represents $20\\%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $20\\%$ of all viewers preferred nature documentaries." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-bee016d0-6cd7-5398-ae5a-81f82544f72f" :question/id #uuid "bee016d0-6cd7-5398-ae5a-81f82544f72f" :question/math-academy-id "q-326891" :question/problem "Find $30%$ of $50,$ and then $20%$ of the result." :question/worked-solution "First, we find $30%$ of $50:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30%\\times 50 & =\\frac{30}{100}\\times 50 \\\\  & =0.3\\times 50 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $20%$ of the result $(15):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20%\\times 15 & =\\frac{20}{100}\\times 15 \\\\  & =0.2\\times 15 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-15fa6bcc-052f-5f93-8f6f-7115563b165d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-15fa6bcc-052f-5f93-8f6f-7115563b165d" :answer-field/id #uuid "15fa6bcc-052f-5f93-8f6f-7115563b165d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6eb478d3-8479-59d5-a04b-887ccad7ef40" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ba290ae-ce34-542b-8844-2cd913434a0b" "answer-7ca6b597-8f66-55e3-a87a-16773b1daf9c" "answer-6eb478d3-8479-59d5-a04b-887ccad7ef40" "answer-17f93f9d-e765-5f23-b7a3-a6bf802d6bbe" "answer-b6a6d2cc-aa72-5e01-a8c2-7be96919829c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ba290ae-ce34-542b-8844-2cd913434a0b" :answer/id #uuid "4ba290ae-ce34-542b-8844-2cd913434a0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ca6b597-8f66-55e3-a87a-16773b1daf9c" :answer/id #uuid "7ca6b597-8f66-55e3-a87a-16773b1daf9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6eb478d3-8479-59d5-a04b-887ccad7ef40" :answer/id #uuid "6eb478d3-8479-59d5-a04b-887ccad7ef40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17f93f9d-e765-5f23-b7a3-a6bf802d6bbe" :answer/id #uuid "17f93f9d-e765-5f23-b7a3-a6bf802d6bbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6a6d2cc-aa72-5e01-a8c2-7be96919829c" :answer/id #uuid "b6a6d2cc-aa72-5e01-a8c2-7be96919829c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e29b2a6a-e1e7-5fde-b63b-dc98de03f40b" :question/id #uuid "e29b2a6a-e1e7-5fde-b63b-dc98de03f40b" :question/math-academy-id "q-327231" :question/problem "Find $110%$ of $80,$ and then $30%$ of the result." :question/worked-solution "First, we find $110%$ of $80:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}110%\\times 80 & =\\frac{110}{100}\\times 80 \\\\  & =1.1\\times 80 \\\\  & =88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $30%$ of the result $(88):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30%\\times 88 & =\\frac{30}{100}\\times 88 \\\\  & =0.3\\times 88 \\\\  & =26.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $26.4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efb48e7b-fc34-5e8f-aab9-f0af854abc24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-efb48e7b-fc34-5e8f-aab9-f0af854abc24" :answer-field/id #uuid "efb48e7b-fc34-5e8f-aab9-f0af854abc24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c9c3b32b-32e4-596f-9422-39b4ac1d3ab8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bfe422f1-e684-5801-92e3-ab70da88986b" "answer-b819777e-a659-5c20-9091-9e7f7829a0d8" "answer-c9c3b32b-32e4-596f-9422-39b4ac1d3ab8" "answer-84d42e1f-305a-54bb-b17d-52bf63e939f0" "answer-b8f9bdda-5a44-5792-bef9-291aa0a56832"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfe422f1-e684-5801-92e3-ab70da88986b" :answer/id #uuid "bfe422f1-e684-5801-92e3-ab70da88986b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b819777e-a659-5c20-9091-9e7f7829a0d8" :answer/id #uuid "b819777e-a659-5c20-9091-9e7f7829a0d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9c3b32b-32e4-596f-9422-39b4ac1d3ab8" :answer/id #uuid "c9c3b32b-32e4-596f-9422-39b4ac1d3ab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84d42e1f-305a-54bb-b17d-52bf63e939f0" :answer/id #uuid "84d42e1f-305a-54bb-b17d-52bf63e939f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8f9bdda-5a44-5792-bef9-291aa0a56832" :answer/id #uuid "b8f9bdda-5a44-5792-bef9-291aa0a56832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-311706e9-5725-57d0-9ebd-1cb5c9f7c783" :question/id #uuid "311706e9-5725-57d0-9ebd-1cb5c9f7c783" :question/math-academy-id "q-327540" :question/problem "An engineer increased a battery’s capacity to $135%$ of its original rating. Then, a safety reserve equal to $20%$ of that new capacity was set aside. If the original capacity was $4000$ mAh, what is the safety reserve in mAh?\n\nThe safety reserve is  \n{{field-1}}\nmAh." :question/worked-solution "First, the new capacity is $135%$ of the original rating $(4000$ mAh$):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}135%\\times 4000 & =\\frac{135}{100}\\times 4000 \\\\  & =1.35\\times 4000 \\\\  & =5400\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the new capacity is $5400$ mAh. Then, the safety reserve is $20%$ of this new capacity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20%\\times 5400 & =\\frac{20}{100}\\times 5400 \\\\  & =0.20\\times 5400 \\\\  & =1080\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the safety reserve is $1080$ mAh." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6430fa47-fc07-5133-b350-c0c171fa758d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6430fa47-fc07-5133-b350-c0c171fa758d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6430fa47-fc07-5133-b350-c0c171fa758d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ec91b8b4-c109-546b-bf90-82bca1add2ef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec91b8b4-c109-546b-bf90-82bca1add2ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec91b8b4-c109-546b-bf90-82bca1add2ef" :answer/id #uuid "ec91b8b4-c109-546b-bf90-82bca1add2ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1080" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e4472fc-358a-5367-8f2d-7c530ac4418c" :question/id #uuid "7e4472fc-358a-5367-8f2d-7c530ac4418c" :question/math-academy-id "q-328004" :question/problem "A museum’s attendance decreased to $80%$ of its previous level. Then, a promotion increased attendance by $25%.$ If the museum originally had $24,000$ attendees, how many attendees were added by the promotion?\n\nThe number of attendees added is  \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, the new attendance is $80%$ of the previous level $(24,000$ attendees$):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}80%\\times 24,000 & =\\frac{80}{100}\\times 24,000 \\\\  & =0.8\\times 24,000 \\\\  & =19,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the new attendance is $19,200.$ Then, the attendees added by the promotion is $25%$ of this new attendance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25%\\times 19,200 & =\\frac{25}{100}\\times 19,200 \\\\  & =0.25\\times 19,200 \\\\  & =4,800\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of attendees added is $4,800.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3e451071-6119-5fde-945d-d4fcf665d96a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e451071-6119-5fde-945d-d4fcf665d96a" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e451071-6119-5fde-945d-d4fcf665d96a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-aad0335b-1731-5695-976a-b24de2193429" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aad0335b-1731-5695-976a-b24de2193429"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aad0335b-1731-5695-976a-b24de2193429" :answer/id #uuid "aad0335b-1731-5695-976a-b24de2193429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a5e4afd-b3bf-55da-bca0-9104ea0bafe7" :question/id #uuid "3a5e4afd-b3bf-55da-bca0-9104ea0bafe7" :question/math-academy-id "q-327574" :question/problem "Fitness class enrollment grew to $180%$ of the baseline. Of those enrolled, $15%$ chose yoga. What percentage of the baseline chose yoga?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the baseline enrollment.\n\nWe're told that enrollment grew to $180%$ of the baseline. Thus, the new enrollment is $1.8x.$\n\nWe are also told that of those enrolled, $15%$ chose yoga. So, the number of people who chose yoga is\n\n$$\n0.15(1.8x)=0.27x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.27x$ represents $27%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $27%$ of the baseline chose yoga." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54555888-2f4a-506a-879f-422748de22f0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54555888-2f4a-506a-879f-422748de22f0" :answer-field/id #uuid "54555888-2f4a-506a-879f-422748de22f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-891a0519-5699-5997-9688-80da5e4b5a77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fe145326-bfbc-57f0-be57-4357a75e5373" "answer-d13a7742-c51e-5d7e-819d-990c72186a10" "answer-891a0519-5699-5997-9688-80da5e4b5a77" "answer-57944d59-4548-51e3-b2bc-f10d7935a6a5" "answer-58e2fcd0-4ea8-5bae-941b-1c3addb5d792"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe145326-bfbc-57f0-be57-4357a75e5373" :answer/id #uuid "fe145326-bfbc-57f0-be57-4357a75e5373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d13a7742-c51e-5d7e-819d-990c72186a10" :answer/id #uuid "d13a7742-c51e-5d7e-819d-990c72186a10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-891a0519-5699-5997-9688-80da5e4b5a77" :answer/id #uuid "891a0519-5699-5997-9688-80da5e4b5a77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57944d59-4548-51e3-b2bc-f10d7935a6a5" :answer/id #uuid "57944d59-4548-51e3-b2bc-f10d7935a6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58e2fcd0-4ea8-5bae-941b-1c3addb5d792" :answer/id #uuid "58e2fcd0-4ea8-5bae-941b-1c3addb5d792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-786bda33-d02b-5551-a3f5-7adb0032f21a" :question/id #uuid "786bda33-d02b-5551-a3f5-7adb0032f21a" :question/math-academy-id "q-327570" :question/problem "A company’s employee count increased to $125%$ of last year’s total. Of these employees, $20%$ work remotely. What percentage of last year’s total now work remotely?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the number of employees last year.\n\nWe're told that the total number increased to $125%$ of last year’s total. Thus, the current number of employees is $1.25x.$\n\nWe are also told that of these employees, $20%$ work remotely. So, the number of employees working remotely is\n\n$$\n0.20(1.25x)=0.25x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.25x$ represents $25%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $25%$ of last year’s employees now work remotely." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06487dff-824c-5b16-9a29-dc375e4d13b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06487dff-824c-5b16-9a29-dc375e4d13b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "06487dff-824c-5b16-9a29-dc375e4d13b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-abe9f14d-e706-5d0a-b03c-1dcc3935a8cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-293d27cb-6be7-542a-a8b8-147db89da707" "answer-d10e3970-e073-5861-9d00-25bade6ebf66" "answer-abe9f14d-e706-5d0a-b03c-1dcc3935a8cd" "answer-39360d96-4ec6-5354-8205-5964ad5fd93c" "answer-e344b716-08e2-5ea2-910b-b5e790292980"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-293d27cb-6be7-542a-a8b8-147db89da707" :answer/id #uuid "293d27cb-6be7-542a-a8b8-147db89da707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d10e3970-e073-5861-9d00-25bade6ebf66" :answer/id #uuid "d10e3970-e073-5861-9d00-25bade6ebf66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abe9f14d-e706-5d0a-b03c-1dcc3935a8cd" :answer/id #uuid "abe9f14d-e706-5d0a-b03c-1dcc3935a8cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39360d96-4ec6-5354-8205-5964ad5fd93c" :answer/id #uuid "39360d96-4ec6-5354-8205-5964ad5fd93c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e344b716-08e2-5ea2-910b-b5e790292980" :answer/id #uuid "e344b716-08e2-5ea2-910b-b5e790292980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230167 :tutorial/content "In many real-world situations, such as in retail or finance, it is necessary to apply multiple percentages in succession.\n\nTo do so, we perform one percentage calculation and then apply another percentage to the *result* of the previous calculation.\nThis means each new percentage is based on a *new amount*, not on the original number.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $40\\%$ of $150,$ and then $25\\%$ of the result.\n\nFirst, we find $40\\%$ of $150{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40%\\times 150 & =\\frac{40}{100}\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.4\\times 150 \\\\  & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after the first step, the result is $60.$\nThen, we find $25\\%$ of the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25%\\times 60 & =\\frac{25}{100}\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.25\\times 60 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after applying both percentages in succession, the final answer is $15.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230171 :tutorial/content "When percentages are applied in succession, it is useful to represent their combined effect as a single percentage of the original amount. \n\nThis means that, instead of applying one percentage and then another, we can multiply their decimal multipliers to find an overall multiplier (or percentage) for the total change. \n\nFor example, suppose that a city’s library membership rose to $150\\%$ of the previous year’s total. Of these members, $40\\%$ borrowed digital books. What percentage of last year’s members borrowed digital books?\n\nFirst, let $x$ be the number of members in the previous year.\n\nWe're told that membership rose to $150\\%$ of the previous year’s total. Thus, the new number of members is \n\n$$\n1.5x.\n$$\n\nWe are also told that of those members, $40\\%$ borrowed digital books. So, the number of members who borrowed digital books is\n\n$$\n0.4(1.5x) = 0.6x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.6x$ represents $60\\%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $60\\%$ of last year’s members borrowed digital books." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229243 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124661 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8bd57c14-ae43-573a-96f9-4a756bc9a869" "question-16c9d9f3-b6b3-5f3f-a06a-81ddff866ad4" "question-881251ae-3ce1-502c-8f83-ef36164a7a11" "question-37a7b0c0-d000-5746-9972-d4929172a0ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124663 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5d186d1a-cd8d-5a4f-8dee-02515d4d8947" "question-22cc12b8-5ddc-5c5a-b8ac-2ac46afb7003" "question-1d359bbd-ffea-5e49-a7be-f90cdd60255a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124664 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9426b3d5-4ce9-5f76-8b8a-628c207151a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8bd57c14-ae43-573a-96f9-4a756bc9a869" :question/id #uuid "8bd57c14-ae43-573a-96f9-4a756bc9a869" :question/math-academy-id "q-35719" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+9}{8{x}^{5}+x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+9}{8{x}^{5}+x} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{9}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{8{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{9}{{x}^{5}})}{(8+\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0}{8+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-51d88423-72f9-55d3-bfd2-ae1d580b9e22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51d88423-72f9-55d3-bfd2-ae1d580b9e22" :answer-field/id #uuid "51d88423-72f9-55d3-bfd2-ae1d580b9e22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd567928-025a-5d7c-a077-128da30f66f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a260e183-6a51-5103-8e98-b97570d9cc31" "answer-cd567928-025a-5d7c-a077-128da30f66f7" "answer-a2ac2659-0176-5b78-a38a-f3cd1c7380d9" "answer-725cde84-240c-5711-867a-be8e0d4bd1a3" "answer-eafe233a-e75a-5307-a7f3-812ec920fd1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a260e183-6a51-5103-8e98-b97570d9cc31" :answer/id #uuid "a260e183-6a51-5103-8e98-b97570d9cc31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd567928-025a-5d7c-a077-128da30f66f7" :answer/id #uuid "cd567928-025a-5d7c-a077-128da30f66f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2ac2659-0176-5b78-a38a-f3cd1c7380d9" :answer/id #uuid "a2ac2659-0176-5b78-a38a-f3cd1c7380d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-725cde84-240c-5711-867a-be8e0d4bd1a3" :answer/id #uuid "725cde84-240c-5711-867a-be8e0d4bd1a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eafe233a-e75a-5307-a7f3-812ec920fd1c" :answer/id #uuid "eafe233a-e75a-5307-a7f3-812ec920fd1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-16c9d9f3-b6b3-5f3f-a06a-81ddff866ad4" :question/id #uuid "16c9d9f3-b6b3-5f3f-a06a-81ddff866ad4" :question/math-academy-id "q-35725" :question/problem "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1-18{x}^{2}}{12p{x}^{2}-3x+9}=-2,$  what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1-18{x}^{2}}{12p{x}^{2}-3x+9} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{18{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{12p{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{3x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-18)}{(12p-\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-18}{12p-0+0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2p} & =-2 \\\\ 4p & =3 \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8fec2a0d-6bd7-5672-995f-b7af0b1f6b11"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8fec2a0d-6bd7-5672-995f-b7af0b1f6b11" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fec2a0d-6bd7-5672-995f-b7af0b1f6b11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9e3277a-6fab-503e-97c7-15fca17a5119" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7be291b6-d083-5af3-8ebc-d5ffcb3774df" "answer-fb11c2f2-7ebe-5372-8d74-0d5f425df3a2" "answer-f27dfe74-1cc3-5f37-8d41-5e6cb0ac0cea" "answer-29005a9b-9b50-5a7c-888b-dcbf8ffed5ad" "answer-e9e3277a-6fab-503e-97c7-15fca17a5119"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7be291b6-d083-5af3-8ebc-d5ffcb3774df" :answer/id #uuid "7be291b6-d083-5af3-8ebc-d5ffcb3774df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb11c2f2-7ebe-5372-8d74-0d5f425df3a2" :answer/id #uuid "fb11c2f2-7ebe-5372-8d74-0d5f425df3a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f27dfe74-1cc3-5f37-8d41-5e6cb0ac0cea" :answer/id #uuid "f27dfe74-1cc3-5f37-8d41-5e6cb0ac0cea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29005a9b-9b50-5a7c-888b-dcbf8ffed5ad" :answer/id #uuid "29005a9b-9b50-5a7c-888b-dcbf8ffed5ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9e3277a-6fab-503e-97c7-15fca17a5119" :answer/id #uuid "e9e3277a-6fab-503e-97c7-15fca17a5119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-881251ae-3ce1-502c-8f83-ef36164a7a11" :question/id #uuid "881251ae-3ce1-502c-8f83-ef36164a7a11" :question/math-academy-id "q-339424" :question/problem "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+1}{3{x}^{4}-x+5}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{4}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+1}{3{x}^{4}-x+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{7x}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}})}{(3-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0}{3-0+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9305cced-9e82-583f-9fb7-1a195ab922a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9305cced-9e82-583f-9fb7-1a195ab922a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9305cced-9e82-583f-9fb7-1a195ab922a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e2c073a3-e98b-5724-bbcf-df8e016578fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e2c073a3-e98b-5724-bbcf-df8e016578fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2c073a3-e98b-5724-bbcf-df8e016578fe" :answer/id #uuid "e2c073a3-e98b-5724-bbcf-df8e016578fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37a7b0c0-d000-5746-9972-d4929172a0ac" :question/id #uuid "37a7b0c0-d000-5746-9972-d4929172a0ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-48839" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{27}{{x}^{3}-8}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{27}{{x}^{3}-8} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{27}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{27}{{x}^{3}})}{(1-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{(1-0)} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a5d64e0e-3da9-53d7-b30f-693879a110d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a5d64e0e-3da9-53d7-b30f-693879a110d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d64e0e-3da9-53d7-b30f-693879a110d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a26ee256-7c9c-5ba6-b063-c02180ed729e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a26ee256-7c9c-5ba6-b063-c02180ed729e" "answer-c660aaf2-fb6a-53fb-b651-7124c2d5503a" "answer-6a3373f2-c4e1-5a17-a5d2-3a3c386494e3" "answer-4d9fedce-bc28-5d24-b746-f2a3ba35b875" "answer-efc8055d-bde7-550e-8883-9ee0d5b41e52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a26ee256-7c9c-5ba6-b063-c02180ed729e" :answer/id #uuid "a26ee256-7c9c-5ba6-b063-c02180ed729e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c660aaf2-fb6a-53fb-b651-7124c2d5503a" :answer/id #uuid "c660aaf2-fb6a-53fb-b651-7124c2d5503a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a3373f2-c4e1-5a17-a5d2-3a3c386494e3" :answer/id #uuid "6a3373f2-c4e1-5a17-a5d2-3a3c386494e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d9fedce-bc28-5d24-b746-f2a3ba35b875" :answer/id #uuid "4d9fedce-bc28-5d24-b746-f2a3ba35b875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efc8055d-bde7-550e-8883-9ee0d5b41e52" :answer/id #uuid "efc8055d-bde7-550e-8883-9ee0d5b41e52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314148 :answer-field/correct "answer-9de6e7b6-7290-559c-ac83-f864f0b80f97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9de6e7b6-7290-559c-ac83-f864f0b80f97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9de6e7b6-7290-559c-ac83-f864f0b80f97" :answer/id #uuid "9de6e7b6-7290-559c-ac83-f864f0b80f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5d186d1a-cd8d-5a4f-8dee-02515d4d8947" :question/id #uuid "5d186d1a-cd8d-5a4f-8dee-02515d4d8947" :question/math-academy-id "q-35765" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{6{x}^{5}}{2{x}^{9}+{x}^{4}+9x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{9}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6{x}^{5}}{2{x}^{9}+{x}^{4}+9x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{6{x}^{5}}{{x}^{9}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{9}}{{x}^{9}}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{9}}+\\frac{9x}{{x}^{9}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}})}{(2+\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{9}{{x}^{8}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{2+0+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-644a0d25-983f-5344-8813-91c7a7069fd3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-644a0d25-983f-5344-8813-91c7a7069fd3" :answer-field/id #uuid "644a0d25-983f-5344-8813-91c7a7069fd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-28f1e747-6d55-5298-ace4-95dd52c7d617" :answer-field/choices ["answer-28f1e747-6d55-5298-ace4-95dd52c7d617" "answer-fb6b5695-1aa2-5966-99ac-6888affc3493" "answer-c50ca5b1-36da-5a46-b3f8-e7b59a548d3e" "answer-3a437750-a172-5976-b64c-d632be99d199" "answer-417e061a-8287-5bae-b9b8-c63d3153875c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28f1e747-6d55-5298-ace4-95dd52c7d617" :answer/id #uuid "28f1e747-6d55-5298-ace4-95dd52c7d617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb6b5695-1aa2-5966-99ac-6888affc3493" :answer/id #uuid "fb6b5695-1aa2-5966-99ac-6888affc3493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c50ca5b1-36da-5a46-b3f8-e7b59a548d3e" :answer/id #uuid "c50ca5b1-36da-5a46-b3f8-e7b59a548d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a437750-a172-5976-b64c-d632be99d199" :answer/id #uuid "3a437750-a172-5976-b64c-d632be99d199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-417e061a-8287-5bae-b9b8-c63d3153875c" :answer/id #uuid "417e061a-8287-5bae-b9b8-c63d3153875c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-22cc12b8-5ddc-5c5a-b8ac-2ac46afb7003" :question/id #uuid "22cc12b8-5ddc-5c5a-b8ac-2ac46afb7003" :question/math-academy-id "q-339637" :question/problem "The horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{-1}{3{x}^{3}+5}$ is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-1}{3{x}^{3}+5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{-1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{-1}{{x}^{3}})}{(3+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{3+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b57aac32-eba8-5f85-9381-a300601e8081"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b57aac32-eba8-5f85-9381-a300601e8081" :answer-field/id #uuid "b57aac32-eba8-5f85-9381-a300601e8081" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7c2c59b0-a796-5757-a453-236cf2d643bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c2c59b0-a796-5757-a453-236cf2d643bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c2c59b0-a796-5757-a453-236cf2d643bb" :answer/id #uuid "7c2c59b0-a796-5757-a453-236cf2d643bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d359bbd-ffea-5e49-a7be-f90cdd60255a" :question/id #uuid "1d359bbd-ffea-5e49-a7be-f90cdd60255a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48838" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}+4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}})}{(1+\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d99197d1-b7c2-5321-bba2-d50ff0c5dd66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d99197d1-b7c2-5321-bba2-d50ff0c5dd66" :answer-field/id #uuid "d99197d1-b7c2-5321-bba2-d50ff0c5dd66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03d97ec7-41c9-58e3-9bad-cd84ac80020c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03d97ec7-41c9-58e3-9bad-cd84ac80020c" "answer-0040223b-3414-5538-888b-8f1cdb82fe50" "answer-4bad6395-c50c-5273-b2cf-20bebd01232a" "answer-b28f6df6-dd1f-5815-9b84-be8a451f93f3" "answer-64bfad7a-0820-50f0-93a5-c290dcf81277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d97ec7-41c9-58e3-9bad-cd84ac80020c" :answer/id #uuid "03d97ec7-41c9-58e3-9bad-cd84ac80020c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0040223b-3414-5538-888b-8f1cdb82fe50" :answer/id #uuid "0040223b-3414-5538-888b-8f1cdb82fe50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bad6395-c50c-5273-b2cf-20bebd01232a" :answer/id #uuid "4bad6395-c50c-5273-b2cf-20bebd01232a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b28f6df6-dd1f-5815-9b84-be8a451f93f3" :answer/id #uuid "b28f6df6-dd1f-5815-9b84-be8a451f93f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64bfad7a-0820-50f0-93a5-c290dcf81277" :answer/id #uuid "64bfad7a-0820-50f0-93a5-c290dcf81277" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9426b3d5-4ce9-5f76-8b8a-628c207151a9" :question/id #uuid "9426b3d5-4ce9-5f76-8b8a-628c207151a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101318" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{6{x}^{3}-x}{{x}^{2}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6{x}^{3}-x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{6{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(6x-\\frac{1}{x})}{(1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(6x-0)}{(1+0)} \\\\  & =6{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ca041ea-2eb0-5b17-ae12-8f4cd24f66d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ca041ea-2eb0-5b17-ae12-8f4cd24f66d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca041ea-2eb0-5b17-ae12-8f4cd24f66d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7325fb68-d309-5a52-b9c3-1f2077dc2892" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18225e1f-0a99-5c73-ba86-725d19891b9b" "answer-4c3b8c2c-22f2-5c5d-b620-41024514bb25" "answer-434a426b-ea91-5826-94d3-a8c38da8e809" "answer-2c78ef0f-8c9a-5e42-bb47-baeca8842914" "answer-7325fb68-d309-5a52-b9c3-1f2077dc2892"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18225e1f-0a99-5c73-ba86-725d19891b9b" :answer/id #uuid "18225e1f-0a99-5c73-ba86-725d19891b9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c3b8c2c-22f2-5c5d-b620-41024514bb25" :answer/id #uuid "4c3b8c2c-22f2-5c5d-b620-41024514bb25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-434a426b-ea91-5826-94d3-a8c38da8e809" :answer/id #uuid "434a426b-ea91-5826-94d3-a8c38da8e809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c78ef0f-8c9a-5e42-bb47-baeca8842914" :answer/id #uuid "2c78ef0f-8c9a-5e42-bb47-baeca8842914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7325fb68-d309-5a52-b9c3-1f2077dc2892" :answer/id #uuid "7325fb68-d309-5a52-b9c3-1f2077dc2892" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124703 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198370 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5787fa90-c666-5c53-9045-790fb21cdab8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5787fa90-c666-5c53-9045-790fb21cdab8" :question/id #uuid "5787fa90-c666-5c53-9045-790fb21cdab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160577" :question/problem "Consider all non-critical points of the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3xy\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}$ and $v(x,y)=3xy.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =3y & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & -\\frac{2x}{{y}^{3}} \\\\ 3y & 3x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot 3x-(-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{3}})\\cdot 3y \\\\  & =\\frac{9x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =9u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9u}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac0df0bc-bf6e-51c0-bdb6-19b9ad7ef142"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac0df0bc-bf6e-51c0-bdb6-19b9ad7ef142" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac0df0bc-bf6e-51c0-bdb6-19b9ad7ef142" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e9a8a63-07dd-5f16-a2f8-3b7c74281739" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b09dc02-1831-530e-86c4-190d1b8a2dbc" "answer-4e9a8a63-07dd-5f16-a2f8-3b7c74281739" "answer-8f5b8a16-21fd-5169-addf-da191e48ae8d" "answer-7766cddb-20aa-5b50-8013-76522352d29c" "answer-9673978f-ee00-5dbf-beeb-1fda93353e40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b09dc02-1831-530e-86c4-190d1b8a2dbc" :answer/id #uuid "6b09dc02-1831-530e-86c4-190d1b8a2dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e9a8a63-07dd-5f16-a2f8-3b7c74281739" :answer/id #uuid "4e9a8a63-07dd-5f16-a2f8-3b7c74281739" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f5b8a16-21fd-5169-addf-da191e48ae8d" :answer/id #uuid "8f5b8a16-21fd-5169-addf-da191e48ae8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7766cddb-20aa-5b50-8013-76522352d29c" :answer/id #uuid "7766cddb-20aa-5b50-8013-76522352d29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{v}{u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9673978f-ee00-5dbf-beeb-1fda93353e40" :answer/id #uuid "9673978f-ee00-5dbf-beeb-1fda93353e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9906dd6e-f368-5644-ad97-3ccd3454dbd9" :activity/id #uuid "9906dd6e-f368-5644-ad97-3ccd3454dbd9" :activity/title "The Inverse Function Theorem" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048251 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-4da312bf-59b4-5062-8ec0-dbcdcb029a0e" "step-4f3a2d34-0995-5368-905a-f5f4b05fda88" "step-85fa7b96-b748-5bcb-8112-da4536f9e0d7" "step-8799c879-5fd1-5dbd-8c44-d6fe6d0c6a5b" "step-4b56f991-f12d-5895-8d7a-a6f922386e67"] :activity/first-step "step-4da312bf-59b4-5062-8ec0-dbcdcb029a0e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-4da312bf-59b4-5062-8ec0-dbcdcb029a0e" :step/id #uuid "4da312bf-59b4-5062-8ec0-dbcdcb029a0e" :step/content 17592186198947 :step/next "step-4f3a2d34-0995-5368-905a-f5f4b05fda88" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4f3a2d34-0995-5368-905a-f5f4b05fda88" :step/id #uuid "4f3a2d34-0995-5368-905a-f5f4b05fda88" :step/content 17592186199003 :step/next "step-85fa7b96-b748-5bcb-8112-da4536f9e0d7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-85fa7b96-b748-5bcb-8112-da4536f9e0d7" :step/id #uuid "85fa7b96-b748-5bcb-8112-da4536f9e0d7" :step/content 17592186383522 :step/next "step-8799c879-5fd1-5dbd-8c44-d6fe6d0c6a5b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8799c879-5fd1-5dbd-8c44-d6fe6d0c6a5b" :step/id #uuid "8799c879-5fd1-5dbd-8c44-d6fe6d0c6a5b" :step/content "question-5787fa90-c666-5c53-9045-790fb21cdab8" :step/next "step-4b56f991-f12d-5895-8d7a-a6f922386e67" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4b56f991-f12d-5895-8d7a-a6f922386e67" :step/id #uuid "4b56f991-f12d-5895-8d7a-a6f922386e67" :step/content 17592186281361 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "knowledge-point-fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" :knowledge-point/canonical-example "question-2ce7e093-c668-5ab6-b343-b49f04300b13" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2514286d-4d63-5e73-b3f0-9f2adecb4d08" "question-ed0dc0e5-67a3-5514-ad15-795a9dd0dc11"] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Additive Inverse" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186408186 :topic/knowledge-points ["knowledge-point-fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" "knowledge-point-056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" "knowledge-point-dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" "knowledge-point-fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" "knowledge-point-fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" "knowledge-point-056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" "knowledge-point-056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" "knowledge-point-056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" "knowledge-point-dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" "knowledge-point-dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" "knowledge-point-dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" "knowledge-point-dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de"] :db/ensure [:topic/identity-validate]} {:db/id "question-2ce7e093-c668-5ab6-b343-b49f04300b13" :question/id #uuid "2ce7e093-c668-5ab6-b343-b49f04300b13" :question/math-academy-id "e-22712" :question/problem "How can we represent the additive inverse of $-2$ on the number line?" :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of a number is the number that lies at the same distance from zero on the number line, but on the opposite side. \n\nAs we can see on the number line below, the distance of $-2$ from zero is $2$ units. The only other number that is at a distance of $2$ units from zero is $2.$\n\n![](images/03/035ad7581b3084ab33917ceb4560b46054871f96551b30825d5c14239a7c0687.png)\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of $-2$ is $2$, and it can be represented on the number line as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75b5ed5f417e89d2ed58f5b2892f43bdbf64ca44da2e7b031a18a9147fd2940a.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "knowledge-point-056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" :knowledge-point/id #uuid "056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" :knowledge-point/canonical-example "question-b716c849-40fa-5f39-a344-ee1a0ebde20d" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ae45fb99-3296-59e3-8a59-381f72003cfe" "question-caba3d37-19c8-51f8-9627-60834d1806c5" "question-ef66e122-a2b4-5616-86af-6621c724508e"] :knowledge-point/title "Adding Opposite Quantities" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b716c849-40fa-5f39-a344-ee1a0ebde20d" :question/id #uuid "b716c849-40fa-5f39-a344-ee1a0ebde20d" :question/math-academy-id "e-22721" :question/problem "A drone’s elevation **dropped by** $85\\text{ m}$ while descending into a valley. Then it **rose by** $85\\text{ m}$ while flying back up.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The drone’s elevation is now higher than the initial elevation.\n\nII. The drone’s elevation is now lower than the initial elevation.\n\nIII. The drone returned to the initial elevation." :question/worked-solution "In our situation:\n\n- While descending, the drone’s elevation *dropped by* $85\\text{ m}$, which is a change of $-85\\text{ m}.$\n\n- While climbing back up, the drone’s elevation *rose by* $85\\text{ m},$ which is a change of $+85\\text{ m}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-85 + 85 = 0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total elevation change* is $0\\text{ m},$ so the drone returns to the original elevation.\n\nSo, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "knowledge-point-dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/canonical-example "question-d5c1d845-4926-5b71-9aaf-b7f1a7983af3" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe75ee40-dd66-5b6a-be0b-41d26c4e980f" "question-b2201c29-9c53-5378-91b2-19915c1b3e60" "question-3e975e85-092f-5a1a-be8e-b7301eb722e2" "question-5daaab8a-c401-527b-849d-4cd75e79ca94"] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Addition Using Absolute Value" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d5c1d845-4926-5b71-9aaf-b7f1a7983af3" :question/id #uuid "d5c1d845-4926-5b71-9aaf-b7f1a7983af3" :question/math-academy-id "e-22722" :question/problem "Let $p=-3$ and $q=8.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" :question/worked-solution "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p = -3$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q = 8$, so the distance we move is $|q| = 8.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *positive*, we move $8$ units to the *right* from $-3.$\n\n![](images/b4/b44a40ef3278f0b31899b7a98695a92e332859b5d0f7badb82a241b1bcbef022.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-3 + 8 = 5.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-2514286d-4d63-5e73-b3f0-9f2adecb4d08" :question/id #uuid "2514286d-4d63-5e73-b3f0-9f2adecb4d08" :question/math-academy-id "q-68908" :question/problem "On which number line does the red dot represent the additive inverse of $-5?$" :question/worked-solution "The only two numbers that are at a distance of $5$ from zero are $-5$ and $5.$ So, $5$ is the additive inverse of $-5.$\n\n![](images/2d/2d418c843ba95e0714b1f744f25ba9b1eb767bf570c2026f7f3bc45bf692cb5b.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n![](images/da/da584206c645e659efb4a1945fd98fe79189136bfdf1dafefe78d2f03dddb3b5.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d09949e-f363-58c9-9819-b83d041be3f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d09949e-f363-58c9-9819-b83d041be3f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d09949e-f363-58c9-9819-b83d041be3f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6eb68a6d-c867-5904-9373-994a393b15f9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84c26d43-35aa-57dc-b8b4-99284f1e4b0b" "answer-11c111ee-623b-5f98-b67a-5acddd9818a6" "answer-368ae5a9-951a-59b7-be56-e6a0231708ce" "answer-7fd9a25c-8088-5154-a98e-359d3b8d9fcd" "answer-6eb68a6d-c867-5904-9373-994a393b15f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c26d43-35aa-57dc-b8b4-99284f1e4b0b" :answer/id #uuid "84c26d43-35aa-57dc-b8b4-99284f1e4b0b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/56/5622481d5e79767acc8821140d5f4a7f6284951fd82d31946776ea8e4b9fd187.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11c111ee-623b-5f98-b67a-5acddd9818a6" :answer/id #uuid "11c111ee-623b-5f98-b67a-5acddd9818a6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5a/5a90fb246b4bc13e1a8bad69f8abb23ebd46a38ad840120be59aff3eee911b99.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-368ae5a9-951a-59b7-be56-e6a0231708ce" :answer/id #uuid "368ae5a9-951a-59b7-be56-e6a0231708ce" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/95/9586014ee21b1f1f6674137e6bf3bee0a771944a1f643f215c513cc3868b067e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fd9a25c-8088-5154-a98e-359d3b8d9fcd" :answer/id #uuid "7fd9a25c-8088-5154-a98e-359d3b8d9fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a9/a911cf9e6ec20bbfa26341c66c27fad2c11df018ef987bb6a5406a5fa49